{"title":"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Sidenote\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Sidenote</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangular</a> array of points, with 5 rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> columns, the points are numbered consecutively from left to right beginning with the top row.  Thus the top row is numbered 1 through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/35672a19103f2ead1f02935bb8450addc3318b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> the second row is numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0fcf01bef88eb69ac4d0a5b94a85a7ad21b913e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67f60ae51ee80fb4164f42c1d86c75a977ae300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> and so forth.  Five points, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958f57cd6b60aaadda77f9daa96d3c2b7c3b2d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, P_3, P_4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df2a7b77439ffdfdb07d9b2a089f7e0ccf9d66f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"16\" /> are selected so that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e97f9c98bedd8b1bba471c213261407511ab9a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i.$\" width=\"10\" height=\"12\" />  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the number associated with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a97d13e759a7d8dcdfbd22b56a1ecde693e05a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />  Now renumber the array consecutively from top to bottom, beginning with the first column.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> be the number associated with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> after the renumbering.  It is found that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293562d7d374882a7d8da7c62aad0e61f41d0123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = y_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78fb5bb02ac2be94e9602160c28c3a1affab0653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = y_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b7d8c37afd66698709d92593e48255bcf2e5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 = y_4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2a19adadec163f03cd9859d855dd1ab16997a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_4 = y_5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab2916c7c2612e03a5dba0b0c88e2ea70f1eb33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_5 = y_3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" />  Find the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4a6d41204181432504f1108ded79e4a49e0e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let each point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be in column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. The numberings for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> can now be defined as follows.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb60fc834ad94fa88f20f574e31b6e74f9a2472c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}x_i &amp;= (i - 1)N + c_i\\\\ y_i &amp;= (c_i - 1)5 + i \\end{align*}\" width=\"142\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We can now convert the five given equalities.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6ded6be156d827fc61026db2817db15fdf71a04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align}x_1&amp;=y_2 &amp; \\Longrightarrow &amp; &amp; c_1 &amp;= 5 c_2-3\\\\ x_2&amp;=y_1 &amp; \\Longrightarrow &amp; &amp; N+c_2 &amp;= 5 c_1-4\\\\ x_3&amp;=y_4 &amp; \\Longrightarrow &amp; &amp; 2 N+c_3 &amp;= 5 c_4-1\\\\ x_4&amp;=y_5 &amp; \\Longrightarrow &amp; &amp; 3 N+c_4 &amp;= 5 c_5\\\\ x_5&amp;=y_3 &amp; \\Longrightarrow &amp; &amp; 4 N+c_5 &amp;= 5 c_3-2 \\end{align}\" width=\"416\" height=\"116\" />\nEquations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> combine to form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c0aa65792f67c78862bb1083444f38fd0e6b590.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = 24c_2 - 19\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\nSimilarly equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737a366a904e00f936f8728869ad8f2587dab46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> combine to form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee6cd01627090227c45a3e3ee787dbb771070220.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[117N +51 = 124c_3\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />\nTake this equation modulo 31\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c350296fd13dab4773e30b3daaff14e6676891.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24N+20\\equiv 0 \\pmod{31}\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />\nAnd substitute for N\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e0442e2a0d7ae32f22e5d309988184465edb7841.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24 \\cdot 24 c_2 - 24 \\cdot 19 +20\\equiv 0 \\pmod{31}\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/98907cca004b6027b057c7a0ed5bd6548d25a10f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[18 c_2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{31}\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> might be is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and by substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20f8c7260003bda4a97722226f2c4602ff30276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 24 \\cdot 7 - 19 = 149$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<pre>Note: In this problem there are two \"groups\" of equations that are linked together, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5456aa005832fe81f1a111836895ef8a06146013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1) + (2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3affc1ba62ee0ab6b0fec59708c64541e09ad66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3) + (4) + (5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />. For your second congruence used to narrow down <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, you can use any one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b18b6b31c22f0e0cffb55953aa00662de0cad02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3), (4), (5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />. Moreover, you can directly solve for N. The other two equations and the alternate continuation are given below:\n</pre>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24eb94f0898b44d80acb722c3c2a58ea91ea0ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73N=124c_4-35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" /> [combined equation]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/675910e534481535308d4a991aff2be55cebd6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73N\\equiv -35\\pmod{124}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" /> [written mod 124]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4cb55d841e6570bb15e4c9493c3bb250fb1173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11N\\equiv -4\\pmod{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> [split the equation mod 4 and mod 31, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b59f90d39a0ef1f8df5193e077695debee5ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv5\\pmod{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> supersedes this equation mod 4]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb508fe1d50b5ab5933632708e23e52ee787f3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2N\\equiv 19\\pmod{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" /> [multiply both sides by 3, simplify]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1bed3009f9744195576337a091898c7289177370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv 25\\pmod{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> [multiply both sides by 16, simplify]\n</p><p>Then use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chinese_Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Chinese Remainder Theorem\">Chinese Remainder Theorem</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b59f90d39a0ef1f8df5193e077695debee5ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv5\\pmod{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> to solve for N. \n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323a95fe3e3168fbc85c30f367b19bc2b49c9b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89N=124c_5-74$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/8/0a8faea87077ebae5511e0abb2bcc5c790bb1194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\equiv 50\\pmod{124}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />\nContinue as above.\n</p><p><br />\nCheck to make sure the values of each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> fit the conditions of the problem.\nThe column values can also easily be found by substitution\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50bf1c1ee5f6b89b60302acac8b47fccea7db8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}c_1&amp;=32\\\\ c_2&amp;=7\\\\ c_3&amp;=141\\\\ c_4&amp;=88\\\\ c_5&amp;=107 \\end{align*}\" width=\"66\" height=\"114\" />\nAs these are all positive and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea3f3f8a046594ac35c41529b32969596bf7922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> is the solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sidenote\">Sidenote</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Sidenote\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we express all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc85328d2a26272e3e1383a563c05994be1d1251.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24c_1=5N+23\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da4c44273610ba8ed7ff8b47ada67ba079fcfb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24c_2=N+19\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c9d619c16e3da0207905099180e5d834cd50c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[124c_3=117N+51\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/17065b86ced3246128f7a1606455eef0489c07f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[124c_4=73N+35\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37ae04460dfc11c64dc541d7041c81784c5b835e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[124c_5=89N+7\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>It turns out that there exists such an array satisfying the problem conditions if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85184d0a24dd577105bb29ec3eb71819f41d1d72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N\\equiv 149 \\pmod{744}\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>In addition, the first two equation can be written <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2e19bcfb8aa6477e18934168c5969f6b1f019c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5mod24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />, and chasing variables in the last three equation gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b720fdf02bfa4656260e65752bb8be1e05c7f07a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89n + 7 = 124e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />. With these two equations you may skip a lot of rewriting and testing. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea3f3f8a046594ac35c41529b32969596bf7922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> still appears as our answer.\n</p><p><br />\n-jackshi2006\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I\" title=\"2001 AIME I\">2001 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p